From: Eduardo Ferreira <eduardo.barbosa@toradex.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dolphin, klamath: drop the A/B altbootcmd default

It switches boot slots, which Torizon (single slot, OSTree rollback)
does not have, so hitting the bootlimit reboots the same broken
deployment. With no default, the Torizon boot script sets its own.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Torizon-specific single-slot OSTree rollback]
Signed-off-by: Eduardo Ferreira <eduardo.barbosa@toradex.com>
---
--- a/include/configs/dolphin.h
+++ b/include/configs/dolphin.h
@@ -55,6 +55,5 @@
 		     "setenv initrd_high; run rescue_load; run rescue_setup; run rescue_exec\0"
 #else
 #define CFG_EXTRA_ENV_SETTINGS \
-	"upgrade_available=0\0" \
-	"altbootcmd=if test ${boot_slot} = 1; then bootslot set b; bootcount reset;bootcount reset; run bootcmd; else bootslot set a; bootcount reset; bootcount reset; run bootcmd; fi\0"
+	"upgrade_available=0\0"
 #endif
--- a/include/configs/klamath.h
+++ b/include/configs/klamath.h
@@ -72,6 +72,5 @@
 #else
 #define CFG_EXTRA_ENV_SETTINGS \
 	"usb_pgood_delay=3000\0" \
-	"upgrade_available=0\0" \
-	"altbootcmd=if test ${boot_slot} = 1; then bootslot set b; bootcount reset;bootcount reset; run bootcmd; else bootslot set a; bootcount reset; bootcount reset; run bootcmd; fi\0"
+	"upgrade_available=0\0"
 #endif
